# src/syncai_robot_state, from SyncAI-Robot-State: the status aggregator that
# publishes syncai_common/RobotState. Managed with vcstool, the same way
# driver-manager.repos manages src/syncai_driver_manager, interface.repos manages
# src/syncai_common and third-party.repos manages src/third-party/.
#
#   vcs import < robot-state.repos          # populate a fresh clone
#   vcs import < robot-state.repos --force  # re-checkout after changing the pin
#
# The key already carries `src/`, so run this from the workspace root without an
# extra `src` argument, or the package lands in `src/src/`.
#
# It left this repository in 2026-10, the second package to go out to its own
# repo and be rewritten against rclrs (Rust) that month -- see
# driver-manager.repos for the first. The ROS surface is unchanged: same package
# name, same `robot_state_node` executable, same `robot_state.launch.py` (which
# still reads [system] robot_id and [map] map from the INI and overrides
# `robot_id` / `base_frame` / `map` with them), so both session specs in
# config/sessions/ did not move. What changed is inside the package:
#
#   - `params/robot_state_params.yaml` is keyed on a bare `/**` instead of
#     `/**/syncai_robot_state`, because rclrs matches a params-file key only when
#     it is exactly `/**` or exactly the node's fully-qualified name -- it does
#     not expand `/**/<node>`. The old key would have matched nothing, and
#     `publish_rate` would have silently gone back to its 10 Hz code default
#     instead of the 1 Hz this stack runs at.
#   - `transform_tolerance` is carried for parity and has no effect. It had none
#     in the rclcpp version either (the lookup is gated by a non-blocking
#     canTransform() at the latest available time), but the port makes that
#     explicit: it looks up in its own in-memory /tf buffer, and it does NOT
#     expire a stale transform.
#   - The WifiStatus -> JSON flattening is serde_json now, not nlohmann/json.
#     That was this workspace's only consumer of `nlohmann-json3-dev`, which both
#     Dockerfiles still install.
#
# `src/syncai_robot_state/` is gitignored -- edit the node in that checkout (its
# own git repo) and commit there, never here; the next --force import overwrites
# anything uncommitted.
#
# Tracks `dev`, that repo's default and working branch, like interface.repos and
# driver-manager.repos.
#
# HTTPS rather than the SSH remote: the repo is public, so the build container
# needs no keys. `git@github.com:chungweeeei/SyncAI-Robot-State.git` is the same
# checkout for anyone who prefers to push over SSH.
#
# Like syncai_driver_manager, this is an `ament_cargo` package and the Rust
# message crates it needs (syncai_common / nav_msgs / sensor_msgs / std_msgs)
# are not generated in this workspace yet -- see driver-manager.repos for the
# whole story. One extra wrinkle here: its `tf2_msgs` dependency is NOT one of
# them. rclrs has no tf2_ros binding, so the node does its own map -> base_link
# lookup off /tf and /tf_static, and the ros-humble-tf2-msgs deb already ships
# generated Rust bindings; only if a future base image stops shipping them does
# geometry2's tf2_msgs have to join the underlay.
repositories:
  src/syncai_robot_state:
    type: git
    url: https://github.com/chungweeeei/SyncAI-Robot-State.git
    version: dev
